WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.331 --> 00:00:02.571
(laughs)

00:00:02.571 --> 00:00:05.461
- It's a little flaccid.
(laughs)

00:00:05.461 --> 00:00:06.741
- Mine has more girth.

00:00:06.741 --> 00:00:10.908
(creaking)
(upbeat music)

00:00:19.638 --> 00:00:20.761
- What are we eating?

00:00:20.761 --> 00:00:22.441
- It's a Whopperrito, Ashley.

00:00:22.441 --> 00:00:24.069
It's a Whopper as a burrito.

00:00:24.069 --> 00:00:25.532
- That's what I thought,

00:00:25.532 --> 00:00:27.132
and I was hoping it wasn't.

00:00:27.132 --> 00:00:28.321
- I like burritos.

00:00:28.321 --> 00:00:29.429
I like burgers.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.863
I guess there's a chance

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:33.308
that the parts could be
greater than the sum,

00:00:33.308 --> 00:00:34.998
or the sum could be
greater than the parts.

00:00:34.998 --> 00:00:36.228
What's the saying?

00:00:36.228 --> 00:00:38.545
- Is it like a burger in my burrito,

00:00:38.545 --> 00:00:40.766
or is it a burrito in my burger?

00:00:40.766 --> 00:00:42.945
- I feel like it's just
gonna taste like a burrito.

00:00:42.945 --> 00:00:44.708
- I hope it tastes just like a burrito.

00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:46.558
- Everything is trying to
become everything these days.

00:00:46.558 --> 00:00:48.566
Instagram's trying to be Snapchat.

00:00:48.566 --> 00:00:50.886
- Burger King's trying to
be Chipotle, apparently.

00:00:50.886 --> 00:00:52.078
I hope I don't get E. Coli.

00:00:52.078 --> 00:00:53.977
This is the laziest rolled burrito

00:00:53.977 --> 00:00:55.071
I've ever seen in my life.

00:00:55.071 --> 00:00:56.915
- So, is it literally
just like a Whopper--

00:00:56.915 --> 00:00:58.054
- Are you gonna take it apart?

00:00:58.054 --> 00:00:59.733
Ooh (groans).

00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:02.054
It's just a smooshed up Whopper.

00:01:02.054 --> 00:01:04.025
- It smells more like a burrito

00:01:04.025 --> 00:01:05.374
than a burger, at this point.
- [Woman In Glasses] Yeah.

00:01:05.374 --> 00:01:06.385
- I know that you're not supposed

00:01:06.385 --> 00:01:07.604
to eat a burrito like this, by the way.

00:01:07.604 --> 00:01:08.823
I just need to get to the middle of--

00:01:08.823 --> 00:01:10.345
- You're eating it like corn on the cob.

00:01:10.345 --> 00:01:11.345
Sure, why not?

00:01:11.345 --> 00:01:12.825
You're not supposed to put a
burger in a burrito either,

00:01:12.825 --> 00:01:13.658
so (beep) it.

00:01:13.658 --> 00:01:14.785
- Oh.

00:01:14.785 --> 00:01:16.074
- How does it taste?

00:01:16.074 --> 00:01:17.236
- It tastes like a Whopper.

00:01:17.236 --> 00:01:18.764
- Oh, I just taste tomatoes.

00:01:18.764 --> 00:01:20.705
- It tastes just like a Whopper

00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:22.284
with a tortilla around it.

00:01:22.284 --> 00:01:23.705
- It's hamburger meat.

00:01:23.705 --> 00:01:25.542
It's disorienting.

00:01:25.542 --> 00:01:26.534
- How many calories is this?

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:27.367
Do we know?

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.314
- I don't wanna know the
nutrition facts, though.

00:01:29.314 --> 00:01:30.943
I do not wanna know what's in it,

00:01:30.943 --> 00:01:32.713
and how many.

00:01:32.713 --> 00:01:35.425
I just said I don't wanna know.

00:01:35.425 --> 00:01:36.258
- Yo, straight up,

00:01:36.258 --> 00:01:37.091
this is delicious.

00:01:37.091 --> 00:01:38.592
It has everything you want.

00:01:38.592 --> 00:01:39.734
It is a burger

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:41.084
inside a burrito.

00:01:41.084 --> 00:01:43.271
Just take my (beep) money.

00:01:43.271 --> 00:01:44.413
- I think yeah, this is progression.

00:01:44.413 --> 00:01:45.604
This is mixing cultures.

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:46.437
- Listen to me.

00:01:46.437 --> 00:01:48.573
If a burger wants to
identify as a burrito,

00:01:48.573 --> 00:01:50.002
who am I to say that it can't.

00:01:50.002 --> 00:01:51.724
- People who wanna keep
a burger inside a burger,

00:01:51.724 --> 00:01:53.785
you're holding this nation back, okay.

00:01:53.785 --> 00:01:55.750
You can't hold back progress.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:56.814
We're doing it, people.

00:01:56.814 --> 00:01:58.265
- First, there was steel.

00:01:58.265 --> 00:01:59.465
Then, there were railroads.

00:01:59.465 --> 00:02:01.564
- [Both] Now, Whopperrito.

00:02:01.564 --> 00:02:02.833
- Get used to this, guys.

00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:04.734
This is the new America,

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:06.745
and it tastes not bad.

00:02:06.745 --> 00:02:09.828
(instrumental music)

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:14.115
(creaking)

